{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"f37363fd8866100062bedffb","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce%40oss.qualcomm.com/","channels":["linux-i2c"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce%40oss.qualcomm.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 1/7] pmdomain: arm: Fix -EINVAL from scmi_pd_set_perf_state() on state 0","messages":{"61eb40e1-1eae-45a3-af65-62eaaf27edc4@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"61eb40e1-1eae-45a3-af65-62eaaf27edc4@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"61eb40e1-1eae-45a3-af65-62eaaf27edc4@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"author":{"name":"Mukesh Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Praveen Talari","address":"praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Sudeep Holla","address":"sudeep.holla@kernel.org"},{"name":"Cristian Marussi","address":"cristian.marussi@arm.com"},{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulfh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"},{"name":"Greg Kroah-Hartman","address":"gregkh@linuxfoundation.org"},{"name":"Jiri Slaby","address":"jirislaby@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Brown","address":"broonie@kernel.org"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"chandana.chiluveru@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"arm-scmi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-serial@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-spi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T06:58:29.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T06:58:29.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 1/7] pmdomain: arm: Fix -EINVAL from scmi_pd_set_perf_state() on state 0","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 8/5/2026 1:27 AM, Praveen Talari wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Currently, scmi_pd_set_perf_state() treats a performance state of 0 as"},{"depth":1,"text":"invalid and returns -EINVAL. As a result, devices attached to SCMI"},{"depth":1,"text":"performance domains can report failures when relinquishing their"},{"depth":1,"text":"performance vote."},{"depth":1,"text":"> The OPP framework use performance state 0 to indicate that no performance"},{"depth":1,"text":"vote is required. For example, dev_pm_opp_set_rate(dev, 0) is commonly"},{"depth":1,"text":"used (by firmware or linux)  when a device is runtime suspended."},{"depth":1,"text":"> A zero performance state does not require any SCMI performance request"},{"depth":1,"text":"to be sent. Treat it as a no-op and return success instead of reporting"},{"depth":1,"text":"an error."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Signed-off-by: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"}],"lineCount":12,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Acked-by : Mukesh Savaliya <mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com>"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"},"d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"author":{"name":"Mukesh Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Praveen Talari","address":"praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Sudeep Holla","address":"sudeep.holla@kernel.org"},{"name":"Cristian Marussi","address":"cristian.marussi@arm.com"},{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulfh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"},{"name":"Greg Kroah-Hartman","address":"gregkh@linuxfoundation.org"},{"name":"Jiri Slaby","address":"jirislaby@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Brown","address":"broonie@kernel.org"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"chandana.chiluveru@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"arm-scmi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-serial@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-spi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T07:24:41.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T07:24:41.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 1/7] pmdomain: arm: Fix -EINVAL from scmi_pd_set_perf_state() on state 0","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On 8/5/2026 1:27 AM, Praveen Talari wrote:\n[...]"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":"  drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c | 2 +-"},{"depth":1,"text":"  1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c b/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 3693423459c9..e390f902a444 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ scmi_pd_set_perf_state(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd, unsigned int state)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \tif (!state)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn -EINVAL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn 0;"}],"lineCount":12,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Won't this cause an issue to other drivers ? how are they going to take action based on changed return value ?"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Remove Acked-by due to this till i give back."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \tret = pd->perf_ops->level_set(pd->ph, pd->domain_id, state, false);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (ret)"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":3,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"},"2c036793-23b3-48d4-834f-9daf8000b2d5@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"2c036793-23b3-48d4-834f-9daf8000b2d5@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"2c036793-23b3-48d4-834f-9daf8000b2d5@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-2-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-2-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"author":{"name":"Mukesh Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Praveen Talari","address":"praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Sudeep Holla","address":"sudeep.holla@kernel.org"},{"name":"Cristian Marussi","address":"cristian.marussi@arm.com"},{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulfh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"},{"name":"Greg Kroah-Hartman","address":"gregkh@linuxfoundation.org"},{"name":"Jiri Slaby","address":"jirislaby@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Brown","address":"broonie@kernel.org"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"chandana.chiluveru@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"arm-scmi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-serial@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-spi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T07:36:36.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T07:36:36.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 2/7] soc: qcom: geni-se: Populate clk_perf_tbl with SE source clock frequencies from perf OPP table","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 8/5/2026 1:27 AM, Praveen Talari wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Currently, on the SA8255P platform, protocol drivers attached via"},{"depth":1,"text":"geni_se_domain_attach() treat each OPP on the perf domain as directly"},{"depth":1,"text":"corresponding to a protocol value such as a baudrate or requested"},{"depth":1,"text":"frequency, and simply request that OPP via"},{"depth":1,"text":"geni_se_set_perf_level()/geni_se_set_perf_opp(). This does not allow"},{"depth":1,"text":"computing a source clock and divider combination for a protocol"},{"depth":1,"text":"requested frequency, unlike the Linux clock managed path which derives"},{"depth":1,"text":"this from se->clk_perf_tbl via geni_se_clk_freq_match(), and then"},{"depth":1,"text":"applies the matched source clock frequency with dev_pm_opp_set_rate()."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Change this by treating the OPP table exposed on the perf domain"},{"depth":1,"text":"device as representing the actual SE HW supported source clock"},{"depth":1,"text":"frequencies, the same role clk_perf_tbl plays for the Linux clock"},{"depth":1,"text":"managed path. Populate se->clk_perf_tbl and se->num_clk_levels by"},{"depth":1,"text":"iterating over this OPP table in geni_se_domain_attach(), so that"},{"depth":1,"text":"protocol drivers on the firmware managed (SA8255P) path can also use"},{"depth":1,"text":"geni_se_clk_freq_match() to pick the closest supported source clock"},{"depth":1,"text":"frequency and calculate the required divider, and apply it with"},{"depth":1,"text":"dev_pm_opp_set_rate() the same way as it is done for the Linux clock"},{"depth":1,"text":"managed path, instead of relying on a direct frequency/baudrate-to-"},{"depth":1,"text":"perf-level mapping."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Signed-off-by: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"}],"lineCount":22,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Acked-by: Mukesh Savaliya <mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com>"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":2,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-2-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"},"de19d0ac-3b3c-494b-a3da-028570989bc7@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"de19d0ac-3b3c-494b-a3da-028570989bc7@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"de19d0ac-3b3c-494b-a3da-028570989bc7@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-3-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-3-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"],"author":{"name":"Mukesh Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Praveen Talari","address":"praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Sudeep Holla","address":"sudeep.holla@kernel.org"},{"name":"Cristian Marussi","address":"cristian.marussi@arm.com"},{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulfh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"},{"name":"Greg Kroah-Hartman","address":"gregkh@linuxfoundation.org"},{"name":"Jiri Slaby","address":"jirislaby@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Brown","address":"broonie@kernel.org"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"chandana.chiluveru@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"arm-scmi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-serial@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-spi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T08:55:04.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T08:55:04.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 3/7] soc: qcom: geni-se: Add helper to set SE clock rate via OPP","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 8/5/2026 1:27 AM, Praveen Talari wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"GENI protocol drivers need a common way to scale the SE source clock"},{"depth":1,"text":"through the OPP framework. However, the device that owns the OPP table"},{"depth":1,"text":"differs depending on how the SE resources are managed. For Linux clock"},{"depth":1,"text":"managed platforms, the OPP table is associated with the SE device,"},{"depth":1,"text":"whereas on firmware-managed platforms it is associated with the"},{"depth":1,"text":"performance power-domain device. This requires protocol drivers to be"},{"depth":1,"text":"aware of the underlying resource management model when requesting"},{"depth":1,"text":"frequency changes."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Introduce geni_se_set_rate(), a common helper that abstracts this"},{"depth":1,"text":"difference and applies the requested frequency through the appropriate"},{"depth":1,"text":"device. The helper automatically selects the performance-domain device"},{"depth":1,"text":"when power domains are attached and falls back to the SE device"},{"depth":1,"text":"otherwise."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Signed-off-by: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"}],"lineCount":15,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Acked-by: Mukesh Savaliya <mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com>"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":3,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-3-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com"},"CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com":{"id":"CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com","messageId":"CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com","references":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulf.hansson@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Mukesh Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Praveen Talari","address":"praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Sudeep Holla","address":"sudeep.holla@kernel.org"},{"name":"Cristian Marussi","address":"cristian.marussi@arm.com"},{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulfh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"},{"name":"Greg Kroah-Hartman","address":"gregkh@linuxfoundation.org"},{"name":"Jiri Slaby","address":"jirislaby@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Brown","address":"broonie@kernel.org"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"chandana.chiluveru@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"arm-scmi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-serial@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-spi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T08:57:59.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T08:57:59.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 1/7] pmdomain: arm: Fix -EINVAL from scmi_pd_set_perf_state() on state 0","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Wed, Aug 12, 2026 at 9:24 AM Mukesh Savaliya\n<mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"On 8/5/2026 1:27 AM, Praveen Talari wrote:"},{"depth":1,"text":"[...]"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"> ---"},{"depth":1,"text":">   drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c | 2 +-"},{"depth":1,"text":">   1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":">"},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c b/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> index 3693423459c9..e390f902a444 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"> --- a/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +++ b/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> @@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ scmi_pd_set_perf_state(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd, unsigned int state)"},{"depth":1,"text":">               return 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":">"},{"depth":1,"text":">       if (!state)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> -             return -EINVAL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +             return 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Won't this cause an issue to other drivers ? how are they going to take"},{"depth":1,"text":"action based on changed return value ?"}],"lineCount":23,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I think it's rather the opposite. With the current returned value\n(-EINVAL) the driver doesn't really know what to do. It tried to drop\nits vote, but that failed - so what can it do?"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Moreover, from genpd point of view, this fixes a real bug as the\naggregation for the performance state becomes incorrect during runtime\nsuspend/resume."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Remove Acked-by due to this till i give back."},{"depth":1,"text":">"},{"depth":1,"text":">       ret = pd->perf_ops->level_set(pd->ph, pd->domain_id, state, false);"},{"depth":1,"text":">       if (ret)"},{"depth":1,"text":">"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":7,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Kind regards\nUffe"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":4,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com","parentId":"d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com"},"779ec0da-4b51-4f8e-a59f-d482f8e8dbaf@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"779ec0da-4b51-4f8e-a59f-d482f8e8dbaf@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"779ec0da-4b51-4f8e-a59f-d482f8e8dbaf@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-0-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","20260805-derive_clk_perf_tbl_from_perf_domain_opp_table-v1-1-61171ab1cdce@oss.qualcomm.com","d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com","CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Mukesh Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulf.hansson@oss.qualcomm.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Praveen Talari","address":"praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Sudeep Holla","address":"sudeep.holla@kernel.org"},{"name":"Cristian Marussi","address":"cristian.marussi@arm.com"},{"name":"Ulf Hansson","address":"ulfh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"},{"name":"Greg Kroah-Hartman","address":"gregkh@linuxfoundation.org"},{"name":"Jiri Slaby","address":"jirislaby@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Brown","address":"broonie@kernel.org"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"chandana.chiluveru@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"arm-scmi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-pm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-serial@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-spi@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T09:13:02.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T09:13:02.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 1/7] pmdomain: arm: Fix -EINVAL from scmi_pd_set_perf_state() on state 0","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 8/12/2026 2:27 PM, Ulf Hansson wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"On Wed, Aug 12, 2026 at 9:24 AM Mukesh Savaliya"}],"lineCount":1,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"[...]"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":3,"text":"--- a/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":3,"text":"+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c"},{"depth":3,"text":"@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ scmi_pd_set_perf_state(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd, unsigned int state)"},{"depth":3,"text":"               return 0;"},{"depth":3,"text":""},{"depth":3,"text":"       if (!state)"},{"depth":3,"text":"-             return -EINVAL;"},{"depth":3,"text":"+             return 0;"},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"Won't this cause an issue to other drivers ? how are they going to take"},{"depth":2,"text":"action based on changed return value ?"},{"depth":1,"text":"> I think it's rather the opposite. With the current returned value"},{"depth":1,"text":"(-EINVAL) the driver doesn't really know what to do. It tried to drop"},{"depth":1,"text":"its vote, but that failed - so what can it do?"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Moreover, from genpd point of view, this fixes a real bug as the"},{"depth":1,"text":"aggregation for the performance state becomes incorrect during runtime"},{"depth":1,"text":"suspend/resume."},{"depth":1,"text":"Got it, thanks Ulf for your explanation and also read your previous comments."},{"depth":2,"text":""},{"depth":2,"text":"Remove Acked-by due to this till i give back."}],"lineCount":20,"maximumDepth":3},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Reviewed-by: Mukesh Savaliya <mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com>"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":5,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com","parentId":"CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com"}},"rootIds":["61eb40e1-1eae-45a3-af65-62eaaf27edc4@oss.qualcomm.com","d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com","2c036793-23b3-48d4-834f-9daf8000b2d5@oss.qualcomm.com","de19d0ac-3b3c-494b-a3da-028570989bc7@oss.qualcomm.com"],"childrenByParent":{"d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com":["CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com"],"CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com":["779ec0da-4b51-4f8e-a59f-d482f8e8dbaf@oss.qualcomm.com"]},"chronologicalIds":["61eb40e1-1eae-45a3-af65-62eaaf27edc4@oss.qualcomm.com","d5d64ea3-9c6f-41f5-adc4-9923381d732b@oss.qualcomm.com","2c036793-23b3-48d4-834f-9daf8000b2d5@oss.qualcomm.com","de19d0ac-3b3c-494b-a3da-028570989bc7@oss.qualcomm.com","CAPx+jO_-1tZfZcjae9shyWcKPsj0fM1SvRzC9_JVOvJr--EeuA@mail.gmail.com","779ec0da-4b51-4f8e-a59f-d482f8e8dbaf@oss.qualcomm.com"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}